# - **Why:** on hardware a qubit decays while it waits, so a fair run counts its waiting time.
# - **Why as late as possible:** a qubit then waits in $\lvert 0\rangle$, which decay leaves unchanged, instead of waiting while it holds part of the pair. Every run is scheduled the same way.
# - **Output:** the ZZ circuit's duration and delays, then its schedule as a timeline: one row per qubit that acts, one block per gate, coloured by gate, and a gap wherever the qubit waits. The long blocks at the end are the measurements.

